      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation (37%):</strong> F9 NO (IRGC does not halt within 6 days) and F8 NO (no formal session by July 22); secondary sanctions stay in force; MOU collapses as nuclear deadline passes without a convened round before Aug 16.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted (45%):</strong> Mixed resolution — F9 YES (72h halt achieved) but F8 NO (session delayed past July 22); Hormuz partial recovery stays below F10 threshold; nuclear track extends fragily toward the Aug 16 MOU deadline.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation (18%):</strong> Both F9 and F8 YES within their horizons; Hormuz approaches F10 threshold (&gt;25/day avg) by late July; a July–August negotiating session restores the MOU track ahead of the Aug 16 window close.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. INSIDE IRAN -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · ~200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>IRNA and Tasnim published parallel statements on July 8 attributing the Hormuz strikes to commercial vessels "failing to comply with maritime deconfliction zones established under MOU Annex B." Iran FM Spokesman Nasser Kanaani held a televised press conference describing IRGC actions as "defensive and proportionate" and specified that the MOU's shipping annex remained "technically in force from Tehran's perspective" pending reversal of US reimposed sanctions. IRIB Prime News broadcast the Kanaani statement on a 90-minute loop before 13:00 Tehran time. → supports <span class="cite">F9</span></p>

      <p>Araghchi, en route to Geneva on July 8, told IRNA that Iran "remains committed to the technical track" of the MOU but that resumed formal sessions required Washington to rescind the reimposed oil sanctions. Tasnim ran a counter-commentary the same day framing the 60-day nuclear window as a US maneuver to delay enrichment progress, not a good-faith freeze — a framing Kayhan had published the day before the strikes. IRNA carried the Araghchi statement without editorial reframing, a departure from the post-strike confrontational register typical in prior escalation cycles. → moved <span class="cite">F8</span></p>

      <p>Press TV broadcast a Mojtaba Khamenei sermon excerpt from July 8 Friday prayers calling the IRGC strikes "the vanguard of the final resistance horizon" with no reference to the MOU or nuclear track. The excerpt reached IRGC-affiliated Telegram channels within 90 minutes and Kayhan ran a July 8 front-page headline — "Hormuz is Ours" — with no ceasefire framing. The gap between Araghchi's technical-track statement (IRNA) and the Khamenei Friday declaration (Press TV / IRGC-Telegram) documents the competing institutional registers active within Iranian state communications as of July 8. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

